anical Garden on the Fjord (Alter Botanischer Garten an der Förde), is a former botanical garden and arboretum located at Düsternbrooker Weg 19, Kiel, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany. It is open daily without charge.","wpu":"Old Botanical Garden, Kiel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_Kiel_Pavillon.jpg/960px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_Kiel_Pavillon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hörn Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.315,"lo":10.135556,"d":1025,"ds":"The Hörn Bridge (German: Hörnbrücke) is a folding bridge in the city of Kiel in the German state of Schleswig-Holstein. The bridge spans the end of the Kiel Fjord (called Hörn) and was designed by Gerkan, Marg and Partners.","wpu":"Hörn Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Hoernbruecke_Kiel.jpg/960px-Hoernbruecke_Kiel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Marine-Regatta-Verein","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.333333,"lo":10.15,"d":1259,"ds":"The Marine-Regatta-Verein (MRV), \"Naval Regatta Union\", is a yacht club of the German Navy. Its main branch is located in the harbor city of Kiel, and it has branches in different states of Germany. This club promotes both sailing and powerboating.","wpu":"Marine-Regatta-Verein","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Burgee_of_the_Marine-Regatta-Verein.svg/960px-Burgee_of_the_Marine-Regatta-Verein.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"German National Library of Economics","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.3383,"lo":10.1561,"d":1938,"ds":"The National Library of Economics (German: ZBW – Leibniz-Informationszentrum Wirtschaft, \"ZBW – Leibniz Information Centre for Economics\", formerly: Deutsche Zentralbibliothek für Wirtschaftswissenschaften) is the world's largest research infrastructure for economic literature, online as well as offline. The ZBW is a member of the Leibniz Association and has been a foundation under public law since 2007.","wpu":"German National Library of Economics","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/ZBW_au%C3%9Fen.jpg/960px-ZBW_au%C3%9Fen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kiel Transmission Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.300556,"lo":10.118333,"d":2931,"ds":"The Fernmeldeturm Kiel (Telecommunication Tower Kiel) is a modern landmark of Kiel in Germany, completed in 1975. The 230-metre-high tower, which is used for directional services and TV, VHF and UHF transmission is not accessible to the public. The basket of this tower, which belongs to German Telekom Inc., has a diameter of 40 metres.","wpu":"Kiel Transmission Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/2020-11-06_-_FMT_Kiel_von_DB0IL_aus.jpg/960px-2020-11-06_-_FMT_Kiel_von_DB0IL_aus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kiel Fjord","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.367778,"lo":10.173056,"d":5344,"ds":"The Kiel Fjord (German: Kieler Förde) is an inlet of the Baltic Sea on the eastern side of Schleswig-Holstein, Germany. Beginning at the Bay of Kiel, it extends inland for about 17 kilometres (11 mi), dividing the Dänischer Wohld from Wagrien. It terminates at the Hörn, a sheet of water in the centre of Kiel.","wpu":"Kiel Fjord","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kiel_Luftaufnahme_02.jpg/960px-Kiel_Luftaufnahme_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Levensau High Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.367778,"lo":10.075833,"d":6360,"ds":"The Levensau High Bridge (German: Levensauer Straßen- und Eisenbahnhochbrücke; short: Levensauer Hochbrücke) is a high level arch bridge that spans the Kiel Canal in the German state of Schleswig-Holstein. Built in 1894 it is the oldest bridge crossing the Kiel Canal. A second bridge nearby, opened 1984, is referred to as Levensau Motorway Bridge (German: Levensauer Schnellstraßenbrücke).","wpu":"Levensau High Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Levensauer_Hochbr%C3%BCcke_-_More_Steel_5.jpg/960px-Levensauer_Hochbr%C3%BCcke_-_More_Steel_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Möltenort U-Boat Memorial","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.3794,"lo":10.1947,"d":7139,"ds":"The U-Boot-Ehrenmal Möltenort (Möltenort U-Boat Memorial) in Heikendorf near Kiel is a memorial site belonging to the German War Graves Commission, commemorating the sailors who died serving in U-Boat units during the First and Second World Wars, along with all victims of submarine warfare. The memorial also honours U-Boat sailors from the Bundeswehr who have been killed in service since.","wpu":"Möltenort U-Boat Memorial","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/U-Boot-Ehrenmal_M%C3%B6ltenort_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Christianspris","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.3914,"lo":10.1861,"d":8092,"ds":"Christianspris or Frederiksort was a Danish fortification somewhat north of the then Danish city of Kiel. In 1632 the Danish king Christian IV initiated the works of making a fortification on a land tongue on the West shore of the Kielerfiord on the Jernved peninsula. The purpose was to secure this land against German troops during the 30-years War.","wpu":"Christianspris","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/Christianspris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Kiel ( KEEL; German: [kiːl] ) is the capital and most populous city in the northern German state of Schleswig-Holstein. With a population of around 250,000, it is Germany's largest city on the Baltic Sea. It is located on the Kieler Förde inlet of the Bay of Kiel and lies in the southeast of the Jutland Peninsula, at the mouth of the Schwentine River, approximately 90 kilometres (56 mi) northeast of Hamburg.","wpu":"Kiel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Ayuntamiento%2C_Kiel%2C_Alemania%2C_2019-09-10%2C_DD_96-98_HDR.jpg/960px-Ayuntamiento%2C_Kiel%2C_Alemania%2C_2019-09-10%2C_DD_96-98_HDR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}